The Example programs tile
user-29a-sd-tcl-the-home-screen
Runs load.examples, which puts SD's example programs into the account's own examples.bp and compiles them, then waits for Enter so the summary can be read. It needs the account's bp.edit: without it the tile is dimmed and says why, and load.examples refuses before anything is written.
Turned off, the tile is missing from this account's home screen and its menu entry cannot be chosen. The person can still type load.examples at a prompt they have; this setting only changes the home screen.
